# Deliberate cost/architecture trade-offs for this single-instance stack.
# Re-triage on the next `trivy config` drift, not on a schedule.

# SNS topics (operational alerts, here and in the keel and status-page
# modules): payloads are alarm names and one-line summaries; a CMK forces
# every publisher principal into the key policy and turns a misconfigured
# grant into a silently dropped message rather than an error.
AVD-AWS-0095

# Delivery bucket: SSE-S3 (AES256) encrypted; it holds build artifacts and
# rendered instance config, and a CMK adds cost and key-policy upkeep for
# the instance role with no meaningful gain.
AVD-AWS-0132

# No WAF in front of CloudFront: one instance behind a private VPC origin
# and a login-gated app; WAF's fixed and per-request cost outweighs the
# exposure for this threat model.
AVD-AWS-0011

# Open egress on the app security group: the instance has no NAT gateway
# and needs outbound IPv6 to arbitrary IRC servers and AWS endpoints, which
# no fixed destination list can enumerate. Ingress is limited to the
# CloudFront VPC origin and the Instance Connect Endpoint
# (modules/network/security_groups.tf).
AVD-AWS-0104
